"settings.help.translateTitle" = "Translate Quick Panel";
"settings.help.translateBody" = "New: a Replace button (⌘⏎) writes the translation straight back over the selected text in the source app. It only appears when you opened the panel on a selection — with hand-typed input there is nothing to replace. Input and result now grow with multi-line text.\n\nPress the translate hotkey (default ⌥⌘L, configurable in Settings → Hotkeys) anywhere — no text needs to be selected. A Spotlight-style window opens: type or paste text and press Return. Tippi detects whether it's German or Spanish and translates it to the other language automatically — no language picker needed. The result is shown for reading and manual copying (⌘C or the Copy button); nothing is inserted or copied automatically, so it never overwrites your clipboard unexpectedly. Press Escape, or click away, to close the window. Runs through your configured AI provider, same as the main hotkey.";
"settings.help.voiceTitle" = "Voice Input";
"settings.help.voiceBody" = "Press ⌥⌘T with no text selected: a mic button appears in the popup. Click to start recording, click again to stop and transcribe — speech recognition (Parakeet or Whisper) runs fully on-device. The transcript appears in the popup; pick an AI prompt or tap \"Insert directly\" to paste as-is.\n\nVoice Instruction: select text first, trigger Tippi, then click the mic button, speak your command and click again (e.g. \"make this shorter\"). Tippi applies it via AI immediately.\n\nDictation mode: turn on “Enable dictation hot key” in Settings → Hotkeys and pick a hotkey (default ⌃⌥⌘M). Press the hotkey to start recording, press again to stop — Whisper transcribes locally and inserts the text at the cursor, with no popup. Avoid system-reserved combos like ⌥⌘D (Dock).\n\nHot key style: dictation accepts either a key combination (the classic style, one press starts, another stops) or a single modifier key such as right Shift. With the single-key style both gestures live on one key: tap it to start and stop as before, or hold it to record only while you keep it down and release to insert. Useful for short dictations where your hand stays on the key. A hold that never sees a release — a physically stuck key — stops itself after five minutes instead of recording indefinitely.\n\nDictation polish (opt-in, v1.8.0+): after Whisper transcribes, Tippi can send the raw text through your active LLM provider to remove filler words (\"um\", \"uh\", \"äh\"), add punctuation, and fix obvious self-corrections — then insert the polished text at the cursor. Toggle in Settings → Dictation → Dictation Mode → \"Polish transcript with AI\". The polishing prompt is fully editable. You can also pick a separate, faster provider just for polish (e.g. Groq for ~800 tok/s or Scaleway for EU-hosted sub-second polish). Short utterances (< 50 chars) skip the polish step. On any LLM failure the raw Whisper transcript is inserted instead — dictation never breaks.\n\nLine breaks and punctuation (e.g. for emails, off by default): Settings → Dictation → “Line breaks and punctuation”. Fixed rules, no AI, so it works with or without polish and for short dictations too: a greeting at the start up to the first comma (“Hi Tom,”, “Dear Ms Miller,”, “Hallo Anna,”, “Hola Carla,”) goes on its own line followed by an empty line, every further sentence on its own line, and a short last sentence with a closing word (“Best regards”, “Thanks and best”, “Liebe Grüße”, “Saludos” …) gets an empty line before it. A sentence with “the following”, “as follows” or “folgende” ends with a colon instead of a full stop. A single sentence without a closing stays as it is, so chat messages are not split up. In terminals and apps on the “Press Return after dictation” list none of this happens, since a line break could send something there. Limits: macOS finds the sentence ends; Tippi deliberately does not split after abbreviations like “Dr.”, “e.g.” or “am 3. Oktober”, so a sentence that really ends in a number with a full stop stays joined to the next. If the dictation has no full stop before the closing, Tippi does not recognise it.\n\nDictation for emails: its own hot key (⌃⌥⌘B by default, change it in Settings → Hotkeys next to dictation). The same dictation, but always with this layout, even with the switch off, and never followed by Return. The recording indicator shows an envelope instead of the microphone. If another Tippi hot key already uses the combination, the setting names it and the hot key stays off. It only works while “Enable dictation hot key” is on.\n\nLive text while recording (v2.22+, off by default): Settings → Dictation → “Show text live while recording”. The recording window shows what you have said so far, updated about once a second; the inserted text is the same. Parakeet only, and it costs one extra recognition pass per second, so leave it off on older Macs. Pick the text size (Normal, Large, Extra large) right below. “Indicator position” sets where the recording indicator appears: top or bottom, each left, center or right. If you switch microphones mid-dictation, for example to AirPods, Tippi keeps recording on the new one; the few seconds while Bluetooth switches are not captured.\n\nDictation language quick switcher (v1.8.1+): the menu bar icon now has a \"Dictation Language\" submenu (Auto / Deutsch / English / Español / Français / 日本語) so you can switch Whisper's source language in one click without opening Settings. The active language is checkmarked. The Settings picker continues to work and stays in sync.\n\nSpeech engines: Settings → Dictation → Speech engine switches dictation between Parakeet v3 (default) and Whisper. Parakeet v3 is a CoreML model on the Neural Engine that is markedly faster and more accurate for German and other European languages than Whisper small. Parakeet downloads its ~600 MB model on first use; the status row in the engine section shows whether the model is missing, downloading (with progress), or ready — including a \"Download now\" button. The toast after every dictation shows which engine actually transcribed (\"… · Parakeet v3\" / \"… · Whisper\").\n\nCancelling & polish cap: pressing the dictation hotkey again while \"Transcribing…\" is shown cancels the run. The AI polish step is capped at 30 seconds — if your polish provider doesn't answer in time (e.g. a large local model still loading), Tippi inserts the raw transcript instead of waiting. For instant polish pick a fast provider (Groq) or a small local model — a 70B via Ollama is overkill for punctuation cleanup.\n\nWith Whisper, download a model in Settings → Dictation before first use. Parakeet downloads its model on the first dictation.\n\nHow far the cleanup goes: it runs deliberately conservatively (low temperature), because its job is the opposite of rewriting — fix punctuation and fillers, change nothing else. The result stays closer to what you actually said. Every other AI feature is unaffected.\n\nPress Return after inserting (v2.16): under Settings → Dictation, use “Add app…” to add the apps where a dictation should be sent right away, like the Claude app. Return only fires if the app is still in front when the text goes in, and not if you cancel the dictation. In terminals, code editors and coding agents Tippi presses Return only if AI cleanup left your text unchanged, and always inserts a single line there.";

